  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Use the following information to answer 1 - 3.</para>
<para>A dining hall had a total of 25 tables: some long rectangular tables and some round ones. Long tables can seat 8
  people. Round tables can seat 6 people. On a busy evening, all 190 seats at the tables are occupied.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="184e64c6-377c-4e02-9606-cd7480609667" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9c791505-e60c-44eb-973f-f57d4b73282f" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="20">
    <problem>
      <para> How many long tables \(x\) are there? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 20 long tables</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5fa93333-4840-443d-bc50-6a8ef54eed8b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="5">
    <problem>
      <para> How many round tables, \(y\), are there? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 5 round tables.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>

<!--Q3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Explain or show how you know how many different size tables there are. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      \(x+y=25\)
      \(8x+6y=190\)
      \(x+y=25\) can be rewritten as \(y=25-x\).
      Substituting \(25-x\) for \(y\) in \(8x+6y=190\) gives \(x=20\).
      If \(x\) is 20, then \(y\) is 5.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<para>Use the following information to answer 4 - 6.</para>
<para>A family bought a total of 16 adult and child tickets to a magic show. Adult tickets are $10.50 each, and child
  tickets are $7.50 each. The family paid a total of $141.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="34b56974-8525-44ca-8e2d-48985e6fd41e" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="cc2d4d6a-4a36-4788-9fc7-3971141afe95" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="7">
    <problem>
      <para> How many adult tickets, \(a\) did they buy? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 7 adult tickets</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1dd8b612-92ac-4aa7-91a0-4742c2f64e91" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="9">
    <problem>
      <para> How many child tickets, \(c\) did they buy? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 9 child tickets.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<!--Q6-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Explain or show how you know the prices of the tickets. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.
      \(a+c=16\)
      \(10.50a+7.50c=141\)
      When the equations are graphed, the intersection of the two lines is at \((7,9)\).</para>
    <para>Use the following information to answer 7 - 9</para>
    <para>At a poster shop, Han paid $16.80 for 2 large posters and 3 small posters of his favorite band. Kiran paid $14.15
      for 1 large poster and 4 small posters of his favorite TV shows. Posters of the same size have the same price.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<para>Use the following information to answer 7 - 9</para>
<para>At a poster shop, Han paid $16.80 for 2 large posters and 3 small posters of his favorite band. Kiran paid $14.15 for
  1 large poster and 4 small posters of his favorite TV shows. Posters of the same size have the same price.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="e34d44d0-d9b2-4e7d-b34c-7d5386926586" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4714c583-5139-44ca-894f-0c09224a2ae9" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4.95">
    <problem>
      <para> Find the price of a large poster, \(l\). </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! $4.95 for a large poster.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6332fd04-018c-42ef-a40b-82ea1f16e951" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="2.30">
    <problem>
      <para> Find the price of a small poster, \(s\). </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! $2.30 for a small poster.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<!--Q9-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Explain or show how you know the prices of the posters. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
    <para>When the equations</para>
    <para>\(2&amp;ell;+3s=16.80\) and \(&amp;ell;+4s=14.15\) are graphed, the intersection of the two lines is at \((4.95,2.30)\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

